1
00:00:00,299 --> 00:00:03,968
Start with four prepared AHV nodes and finish with a configured

2
00:00:03,968 --> 00:00:07,339
cluster. ZTF-Orchestrator brings deployment,

3
00:00:07,339 --> 00:00:10,990
post-configuration and verification into one console.

4
00:00:10,994 --> 00:00:14,962
This walkthrough uses anonymised demonstration data, with deployment

5
00:00:14,962 --> 00:00:16,978
progress accelerated for teaching.

6
00:00:17,053 --> 00:00:19,346
It does not measure real deployment time.

7
00:00:19,527 --> 00:00:21,958
From Start Here, choose Deploy a Cluster.

8
00:00:22,148 --> 00:00:26,276
Select the workflow that matches your deployment service: Foundation VM

9
00:00:26,330 --> 00:00:30,287
for a classic local or remote Foundation VM, Cluster Create

10
00:00:30,298 --> 00:00:33,833
for Foundation Central associated with Prism Central, or

11
00:00:33,833 --> 00:00:37,726
Standalone FCA for a separate Foundation Central Appliance.

12
00:00:37,929 --> 00:00:41,460
Each path needs its own reviewed configuration and compatible

13
00:00:41,470 --> 00:00:45,308
environment. Our example follows the Foundation VM path.

14
00:00:45,455 --> 00:00:49,327
Select the intended nodes, check their management addresses and credential

15
00:00:49,381 --> 00:00:53,509
references, and choose the approved AOS and AHV images

16
00:00:53,647 --> 00:00:55,749
already in Foundation inventory.

17
00:00:55,823 --> 00:00:59,620
Refresh inventory and review the available validation results.

18
00:00:59,853 --> 00:01:03,981
Confirm the exact physical targets and satisfy the required approval before

19
00:01:04,034 --> 00:01:07,416
imaging. Open Jobs and Queue to follow deployment.

20
00:01:07,533 --> 00:01:11,350
Watch the reported phases advance through imaging and cluster formation.

21
00:01:11,604 --> 00:01:13,748
The progress sequence is condensed here;

22
00:01:13,780 --> 00:01:15,817
the real job can take much longer.

23
00:01:16,041 --> 00:01:19,785
When formation finishes, verify the expected cluster identity,

24
00:01:19,838 --> 00:01:22,908
membership and health before starting post-configuration.

25
00:01:23,191 --> 00:01:26,989
Open the saved ZTF one point x pipeline and review the

26
00:01:26,989 --> 00:01:29,581
configuration filenames in execution order.

27
00:01:29,719 --> 00:01:32,994
The first nine steps are your post-configuration sequence.

28
00:01:33,133 --> 00:01:36,544
The final three operations use their own governed workflows.

29
00:01:36,691 --> 00:01:40,563
They are part of the same deployment runbook, but this walkthrough does not present

30
00:01:40,617 --> 00:01:43,803
them as twelve automatically chained pipeline actions.

31
00:01:44,235 --> 00:01:48,107
Step one, initial configuration admin password, replaces

32
00:01:48,118 --> 00:01:51,009
the initial Prism Element administrator password.

33
00:01:51,105 --> 00:01:54,934
Verify the replacement login before later steps use its saved credential

34
00:01:54,987 --> 00:01:58,677
reference. Keep password values hidden throughout the demonstration.

35
00:01:59,058 --> 00:02:02,716
Step two accepts the EULA and applies the reviewed Pulse setting.

36
00:02:02,940 --> 00:02:06,066
Step three configures the Data Services IP address.

37
00:02:06,183 --> 00:02:09,425
Step four applies the intended high availability policy.

38
00:02:09,617 --> 00:02:12,764
Step five sets rebuild capacity reservation.

39
00:02:12,988 --> 00:02:16,785
Check the resulting settings rather than treating a successful process exit as the

40
00:02:16,785 --> 00:02:20,732
only evidence. Step six creates the reviewed storage containers.

41
00:02:20,861 --> 00:02:24,615
Step seven sets the Prism Element login title so operators can

42
00:02:24,615 --> 00:02:26,333
recognise the target cluster.

43
00:02:26,535 --> 00:02:30,081
Step eight runs your reviewed Configure Dark Site configuration.

44
00:02:30,235 --> 00:02:32,827
Its source and settings are site-specific;

45
00:02:33,008 --> 00:02:35,558
confirm they suit the installed environment.

46
00:02:35,696 --> 00:02:39,781
The filename is your supplied configuration label, not a claim that every

47
00:02:39,792 --> 00:02:42,559
installation includes an identical built-in action.

48
00:02:42,833 --> 00:02:46,001
Step nine registers Prism Element with Prism Central.

49
00:02:46,076 --> 00:02:48,305
Verify registration on both sides.

50
00:02:48,422 --> 00:02:52,209
If a step fails, inspect its output and reconcile the actual

51
00:02:52,305 --> 00:02:54,065
target state before continuing.

52
00:02:54,097 --> 00:02:56,993
Registration is step nine in this demonstration.

53
00:02:57,180 --> 00:03:00,839
Do not confuse it with the separate recovery baseline whose registration-only

54
00:03:00,850 --> 00:03:03,129
retry is called step zero eight.

55
00:03:03,367 --> 00:03:07,452
After the pipeline checks pass, open AHV Uplink Migration.

56
00:03:07,548 --> 00:03:10,852
Discover the cluster, then review each host individually.

57
00:03:11,021 --> 00:03:14,935
For this example, retain two physical uplinks on v-switch zero

58
00:03:15,074 --> 00:03:17,175
and move two to v-switch one.

59
00:03:17,293 --> 00:03:19,575
Create the destination switch if needed.

60
00:03:19,787 --> 00:03:23,745
The selected NICs must match the actual cabling and management path;

61
00:03:23,883 --> 00:03:25,864
their names can differ between hosts.

62
00:03:26,017 --> 00:03:30,028
Run read-only preflight, review the exact assignments and obtain

63
00:03:30,028 --> 00:03:33,936
approval. The workflow applies one host at a time and verifies

64
00:03:33,936 --> 00:03:36,251
the retained and destination uplinks.

65
00:03:36,411 --> 00:03:40,112
A failed or uncertain result stops the sequence for investigation.

66
00:03:40,208 --> 00:03:44,042
It does not justify automatically replaying completed host changes.

67
00:03:44,403 --> 00:03:48,104
Step eleven changes the virtual switch MTU using the dedicated

68
00:03:48,115 --> 00:03:52,040
workflow. The current action targets v-switch zero and still

69
00:03:52,040 --> 00:03:55,779
uses Prism Central. Confirm jumbo-frame support across the

70
00:03:55,779 --> 00:03:59,491
intended physical network, review the target MTU, then

71
00:03:59,491 --> 00:04:02,297
approve and verify each host's readback.

72
00:04:02,435 --> 00:04:06,190
An optional Prism Element TLS exception does not remove Prism

73
00:04:06,190 --> 00:04:09,656
Central certificate requirements. Check end-to-end traffic

74
00:04:09,656 --> 00:04:13,667
separately. Step twelve enables Data-at-Rest Encryption through

75
00:04:13,667 --> 00:04:17,628
the DARE wizard. Choose the PE-direct path where appropriate,

76
00:04:17,660 --> 00:04:21,788
review local key-manager readiness and confirm licensing and key recovery

77
00:04:21,799 --> 00:04:25,127
ownership. Complete preflight and approval before enabling

78
00:04:25,127 --> 00:04:29,238
encryption. Software encryption cannot be disabled afterward.

79
00:04:29,334 --> 00:04:33,291
Verify the reported encryption configuration, follow background progress

80
00:04:33,387 --> 00:04:35,708
and complete the key-backup procedure.

81
00:04:35,945 --> 00:04:39,870
Finish by reviewing the deployment job, each pipeline result and the three

82
00:04:39,870 --> 00:04:43,401
finishing workflows. Record cluster identity, health,

83
00:04:43,454 --> 00:04:47,198
registration, uplink assignments, MTU and encryption

84
00:04:47,209 --> 00:04:51,002
evidence. The outcome is a repeatable deployment sequence with

85
00:04:51,002 --> 00:04:55,013
visible checkpoints, and a clear record of what completed and what

86
00:04:55,013 --> 00:04:56,451
still needs attention.
